+## [Unreleased] - Part 2: Shizuku engine
+
+> **Still not compiled or run.** Written in an environment with no Android SDK, Gradle, Kotlin compiler or network.
+> The new tests have not been executed. See `docs/PART2_HANDOFF.md` and `docs/SHIZUKU_CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md`.
+
+### Security
+- Typed maintenance requests replace "path + mode": the executor derives the target from a validated package identifier.
+- The service refuses paths with a symlink among their ancestors, refuses tree deletes until the installed-apps guard has been pushed, and never removes CleanForge's own folders.
+- `PackageInventory.installState()` is tri-state; a failed package-manager query is `UNKNOWN`, which skips the item instead of reading as "not installed" (the unsafe answer for a leftover). Folder names are matched to known packages case-insensitively.
+
+### Fixed
+- Backend reads no longer collapse missing / refused / dead service into `null`; a dead service is no longer reported as "Already gone" and a failed scan no longer looks like an empty one.
+- Partial cleanups, limit stops and cancellations keep the bytes that were really freed; a reported success is checked afterwards and downgraded to partial or unconfirmed if the end state says otherwise.
+- Binding: a fresh `ServiceConnection` per attempt, bind deadline, removal of a half-started service, protocol version check, rebinding after death or after Shizuku restarts.
+- "Don't ask again" is detected; the permission button no longer pretends to ask.
+- A service that hangs no longer hangs the app: calls have deadlines, a deadline restarts the service, caller cancellation stops a running delete between entries.
+- A cleanup that throws or is stopped keeps an honest partial report instead of discarding it.
+- Shizuku status checks and capability probes no longer run on the main thread.
+
+### Added
+- Capability registry (per operation: verified / ready / needs permission / unavailable / unsupported), shown on the Shizuku card.
+- `PrivilegedExecutor`: one entry point for privileged work, bounded concurrency, timeouts, structured results (success, partial, failure, unsupported, unverified).
+- Size quality: measured or lower bound (`≥`), unreadable-folder count; scanners report what they could not check.
+- Stop button on the cleaning dialog; report shows partly cleaned and unconfirmed items.
+- AIDL methods 6 to 12 (append-only); methods 2 to 5 unchanged.
+- 120 new or extended unit tests (91 before, 211 now; not run). `docs/SHIZUKU_CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md`, `docs/SHIZUKU_SETUP_AND_COMPATIBILITY.md`.
+
